  "term": "Angelman syndrome",
  "definition": "Angelman syndrome is a genetic condition marked by intellectual disability along with problems in movement and muscle control. Common features include developmental and motor delay, unsteady or jerky movements, low muscle tone, frequent laughter episodes, and distinctive physical abnormalities.",
